<section id="leadership-892">
    <div class="cs-divider-wrapper">
        <div class="cs-divider"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-container">
        <h2 class="cs-title">My Approach & Philosophies</h2>
        <ul class="cs-item-group">
            <li class="cs-item">
                <span class="cs-marker">01</span>
                <div class="cs-text-group">
                    <h3 class="cs-h3">Be scrappy.</h3>
                    <p class="cs-item-text">
                        To be scrappy is to be resourceful and unafraid to get your hands dirty. Start now, with what you have. 
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
             <li class="cs-item">
                <span class="cs-marker">02</span>
                <div class="cs-text-group">
                    <h3 class="cs-h3">Iterate.</h3>
                    <p class="cs-item-text">
                        Learn by doing. No one's qualified to do something until they've done it. Each iteration is growth.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="cs-item">
                <span class="cs-marker">03</span>
                <div class="cs-text-group">
                    <h3 class="cs-h3">Trust your gut.</h3>
                    <p class="cs-item-text">
                        Gather information, ask questions, seek advice and feedback. Then, trust the knowledge you have and your instincts to make a decision.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
           
            <li class="cs-item">
                <span class="cs-marker">04</span>
                <div class="cs-text-group">
                    <h3 class="cs-h3">Simple is superior.</h3>
                    <p class="cs-item-text">
                        "Genius is making complex ideas simple, not making simple ideas complex." - Albert Einstein. It's easy to overcomplicate things when you're overthinking them. Aim for the simplest solution.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="cs-item">
                <span class="cs-marker">05</span>
                <div class="cs-text-group">
                    <h3 class="cs-h3">Most things are fixable.</h3>
                    <p class="cs-item-text">
                        Many times we paralyze ourselves because we're afraid of making a mistake. Fear and self-doubt cloud our thinking. The reality is that most of the things we deal with are fixable. If a mistake is made, it can be corrected.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="cs-item">
                <span class="cs-marker">06</span>
                <div class="cs-text-group">
                    <h3 class="cs-h3">Keep it human.</h3>
                    <p class="cs-item-text">
                        Stale. Corporate. Inflexible. The way we work and the structures we create are changing. Old ways of doing business are dying and what the future asks for is something alive, human, deeply honest, and sustainable.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<script>
(() => {
    const observerOptions = {
        threshold: 0.2,
        rootMargin: '0px'
    };

    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        entries.forEach(entry => {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                entry.target.classList.add('cs-visible');
                observer.unobserve(entry.target);
            }
        });
    }, observerOptions);

    const container = document.querySelector('#leadership-892 .cs-container');
    if (container) observer.observe(container);
})();
</script>

